! >>> THE REFUSAL IS GONE, 2026-11-16, AND THIS DECK NOW PINS ITS
! ABSENCE. <<<  Decimal LFT and DCV were the last two decimal VFL
! operations the model refused; both are built (decks/vfl_lft_decimal.
! strap, decks/vfl_dcv.strap), and the gate (StretchVFL's
! vflDecimalBuilt, asked by execute() and by the I-box's prepareExec) was
! removed in the same change, because it was true of every code.  The
! "BZOP, $" below is now "BOP, $": the decimal LFT must NOT set OP, and
! FT must hold what printed p.69 puts there -- LFT(D,32,8) of the bytes
! 01 02 03 08 is -123, FT = (16)1238 (numeric 123 above a four-bit sign
! byte whose leftmost bit is the sign).  The file keeps its name because
! run_tests.sh and docs/ebox_roadmap.md cite it; everything below this
! paragraph is the history it pinned.
!
! THE DECIMAL REFUSAL IS A MODEL SCOPE BOUNDARY, NOT IBM SEMANTICS, and
! this deck is labelled that way on purpose.
!
! The real 7030 performs decimal VFL arithmetic.  THIS MODEL DOES NOT,
! and refuses it with indicator OP (operation code invalid) so that an
! unimplemented operation is a VISIBLE refusal rather than a silent
! wrong answer -- the same choice bsv/README.md's scope list records for
! every other unbuilt operation.  What this deck pins is therefore the
! MODEL's documented boundary; it must not be read as a statement about
! the machine.
!
! The three RADIX CONVERSIONS are deliberately exempt and are tested
! elsewhere (decks/load_converted.strap, decks/vfl_convert.strap): for
! LCV, CV and LTRCV the decimal bit SELECTS A DIRECTION rather than
! asking for decimal arithmetic -- Reference Manual printed p.72, "If
! this bit is zero, the original field is binary; if this bit is one,
! the original field is decimal" -- so refusing them was refusing the
! operation's normal case.  See StretchExecute's `radixConv`.
!
! A DECIMAL UNSIGNED STORE IS NOT REFUSED since 2026-11-08: MCP's $TIME
! needs it (decks/vfl_st_decimal.strap).  This deck stored ST(DU,32,8)
! until then, and then the signed form.
!
! AND SINCE 2026-11-16 (G2.3 stage 1) NO DECIMAL STORE, LOAD OR ADD IS
! REFUSED (decks/vfl_decimal_add.strap), so the refused operation is now
! LFT(D,32,8), LOAD FACTOR with the decimal modifier: binary LFT is
! built, decimal LFT is not (StretchVFL's vflDecimalBuilt lists what is).
! It fetches, so it is still the "decimal refusal" cause of
! completesWithoutFetch.  The refused_* checks now say only that nothing
! was stored at TB, which an LFT would not do anyway; FT_unchanged says
! the factor register was not loaded.
!
! WHY IT NEEDED A DECK: it is one of the six causes of
! StretchIBox's prepareExec.completesWithoutFetch, and a census of which
! causes the corpus reaches (docs/ebox_roadmap.md) found this one and
! progressive-indexing-with-X0 firing ZERO times in 5621 checks.  Both
! were reasoned from the arms rather than measured.
!
! THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS THE POINT: the legal BINARY store runs first
! and its target is checked for the value it must have, so the deck
! cannot pass by doing nothing at all.
!
! TIMING RE-PINNED 2026-11-16, every value check unchanged. VFL E-box
! time now depends on the operation: bsv/StretchTiming.bsv's eboxClocks
! charges each operation the throughput Perf. Char. Vol. 2's atlas prints
! for it (docs/atlas_oracle.md). A refused decimal operation is charged
! like a run one.
!   - While the refused form was ST(D,32,8), the pin went 140 -> 163.
!     ST's law is PDF 124, 18 + 2 bytes: 26 clocks here.
!   - On the LFT(D,32,8) form this deck now refuses, the pin was 161
!     under the old generic times and is 224 now. The decimal LFT is
!     charged PDF 122's decimal figure, 66 clocks (19.81 us). L(BU,32,8)
!     is charged PDF 120 and the binary ST PDF 124.
! The 224 is the measured count. The 63-clock rise was not taken apart
! by operation.
!   - Since the refusal went (paragraph at the top) the decimal LFT
!     EXECUTES, from TD (one word) instead of TB+.48 (a crossing field):
!     223, measured on the merged tree 2026-11-16.  (The "161 -> 160" of
!     the same change was on the old generic times.)
!
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   L(BU,32,8), DATA1
        ST(BU,32,8), TA+.48          ! legal: binary unsigned
        BOP, $                       ! hang if OP came on: that one is legal
        LFT(D,32,8), TD              ! DECIMAL LOAD FACTOR: built 2026-11-16
        BOP, $                       ! hang if OP came on: it is legal now
        TI, 1, $FT, FTS              ! the factor register, loaded
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
DATA1   DD(BU,32), (16)12345678
        SLC, (8)410.0
TA      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)420.0
TB      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)430.0
FTS     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
TD      DD(BU,64), (16)0102030800000000  ! 1 2 3, sign byte 00001000: -123
        END, START
